Date: 5 August 2026

Time Taken: 1 hour

Skills Learnt:
1. Setting breakpoints in GDB.
2. Examining memory using the x command.
3. Understanding little-endian byte order.
4. Reading values stored on the stack.

Notes:
This challenge required examining how a value was stored in memory instead of reading it directly from a register. I used GDB to set a breakpoint after the value was written to the stack and inspected the memory using the x/4xb command. This helped me understand little-endian byte ordering and how values are stored differently in memory compared to how they appear in assembly instructions.

Commands Practised:
- gdb
- disassemble main
- break
- run
- x/4xb
